<h2 id=3D"AI-323:AI+IntegrationofMilvus-Multi-TenancyandSharding">Multi-Ten=
ancy and Sharding</h2>
<p>For applications that need to serve multiple independent users or worklo=
ads, or for managing very large datasets, multi-tenancy and sharding are im=
portant features. Milvus supports sharding and partitioning, which enable e=
fficient resource utilization and the isolation of workloads from different=
 sources, such as different clients or time-based partitions. Sharding invo=
lves dividing the dataset across multiple independent nodes, while partitio=
ning involves dividing a single collection into multiple smaller segments. =
Both techniques can improve query performance and manageability for large d=
atasets.</p>
<p>ChromaDB, in its current single-node architecture, lacks built-in shardi=
ng capabilities. While partitioning of data might be possible at an applica=
tion level, the absence of native sharding can lead to performance degradat=
ion as the dataset size grows very large. Implementing multi-tenancy, where=
 different users or applications can securely and independently access the =
database, would also be more challenging without built-in sharding and isol=
ation mechanisms.</p>
